@title Yu-Gi-Oh! - The Eternal Duelist Soul (USA)
@file Yu-Gi-Oh! - The Eternal Duelist Soul (U) [!].gba
@game AY5E
@chip SRAM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@known * checkpoint title: -- §33, §29: the references under-charge the boot load, so their title lands a frame early
@known * ~checkpoint continue_title differs from the references -- §33, §29: the same boot-load frame after a load
@known * checkpoint duel_field: -- §88, §33: the first turn's rock-paper-scissors draws from an RNG one step behind since the boot load's frame (f582); both references throw rock and DRAW, replay a round (start_duel SLIP +40) and shuffle another hand. Poking dingbat's RNG word into mGBA at f2441 makes it draw both checkpoints as dingbat
@known * audio differs from both references -- §88, §33: after the references' DRAW their run is a rock-paper-scissors round (40 frames) later; every flagged window is from f2565 on
# New Game, Tea's intro, pick the red starter deck. The game writes its SRAM save right
# after the intro (before the first duel), so [new] ends on the first duel's field and
# [load] Continues into the main menu (Campaign / Link Battle / Deck Edit ...) and opens Deck Edit.
# Notes: before the duel a rock-paper-scissors round (f2446) decides who goes first.
# The opponent's throw and the deck shuffle come from the per-frame RNG at 0x03000040,
# which dingbat steps once less from f582 (the boot load, §33): dingbat wins, both
# references draw and replay a round, 40 frames (two taps), then deal another hand
# (docs/playtest-bugs.md §88). That is why the duel itself is not played here.
# At f1466 the fade-out after picking the deck is at a different step on each emulator.
# Title screen (f854/f884, both [new] and [load]): mgba and nba are pixel-identical,
# but dingbat-bios differs on every row. The green grid background is offset by about
# one pixel horizontally (shifting dingbat-bios by 1 px cuts the differing pixels from
# 13370 to 10577, so it is not only a shift), and the logo and menu text look the same.
# Explained 2026-10-02 (docs/playtest-bugs.md, "Yu-Gi-Oh! ... the title a frame late"):
# a boot load loop (f575-582, EWRAM ldrb from gamepak code) costs dingbat 72.6
# cycles an iteration, mgba 64.8 (below the bus floor), so dingbat is a frame
# behind from f582; the grid is mgba's previous frame and the emblem's flame
# rests 2 px right. Same in [load] with any save.

[new]
wait 600
# until notblank timeout=1500 every=10  [reached dingbat-bios+50 mgba+50 nba+50]
wait 54
wait 200
checkpoint title window=30
press A
wait 120
tap A times=15 every=20 hold=4
checkpoint deck_choice window=30
press A
wait 60
wait 60
tap A times=20 every=20 hold=4
tap A times=20 every=20 hold=4
tap A times=30 every=20 hold=4
checkpoint start_duel window=30
wait 120
checkpoint duel_field window=30

[load]
wait 600
# until notblank timeout=1500 every=10  [reached dingbat-bios+50 mgba+50 nba+50]
wait 54
wait 200
checkpoint continue_title window=30
press A
wait 150
wait 30
checkpoint resumed_menu window=30
press DOWN
wait 20
press DOWN
wait 20
press A
wait 90
checkpoint deck_edit window=30
